If we have a set of intervals, and we start at $X$, we want to know how many times we land in an interval.
Since the rating increases, we move to the right.
Specifically, if we are at $r$, and we encounter an interval $[L_i, R_i]$ such that $L_i \le r \le R_i$, we jump to $r+1$.
Then we check the next interval.
